  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Colossians",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 3,
    "summary": "Some lives are hidden with God in Christ—The Saints are told to be holy and to serve the Lord Jesus Christ.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "If ye then be risen with Christ, seek those things which are above, where Christ sitteth on the right hand of God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 19,
            "text": "Col. 2:12."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Set your affection on things above, not on things on the earth.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "GR mind."
          },
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "Matt. 6:33."
          },
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 34,
            "text": "Prov. 15:24."
          },
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 62,
            "text": "TG Worldliness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For ye are dead, and your life is hid with Christ in God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "Rom. 6:5 (2–5); Col. 2:20."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "When Christ, who is our life, shall appear, then shall ye also appear with him in glory.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "Ether 4:12."
          },
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "1 Jn. 3:2."
          },
          {
            "start": 82,
            "end": 87,
            "text": "1 Cor. 15:43 (42–44)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 19
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Mortify therefore your members which are upon the earth; fornication, uncleanness, inordinate affection, evil concupiscence, and covetousness, which is idolatry:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 7,
            "text": "Rom. 8:13."
          },
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 30,
            "text": "Rom. 6:13."
          },
          {
            "start": 83,
            "end": 103,
            "text": "TG Sexual Immorality."
          },
          {
            "start": 129,
            "end": 141,
            "text": "TG Covet."
          },
          {
            "start": 152,
            "end": 160,
            "text": "TG Idolatry."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For which things’ sake the wrath of God cometh on the children of disobedience:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 32,
            "text": "TG God, Indignation of."
          },
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 78,
            "text": "TG Disobedience."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "In the which ye also walked some time, when ye lived in them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "GR formerly."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But now ye also put off all these; anger, wrath, malice, blasphemy, filthy communication out of your mouth.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 19,
            "text": "Eph. 4:22 (22–24)."
          },
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "TG Anger."
          },
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "TG Malice."
          },
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 66,
            "text": "TG Blaspheme."
          },
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 88,
            "text": "TG Profanity."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Lie not one to another, seeing that ye have put off the old man with his deeds;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 3,
            "text": "TG Honesty; Lying."
          },
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 59,
            "text": "Rom. 6:6; Mosiah 3:19."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And have put on the new man, which is renewed in knowledge after the image of him that created him:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 27,
            "text": "TG Man, New, Spiritually Reborn."
          },
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 74,
            "text": "Rom. 8:29."
          },
          {
            "start": 87,
            "end": 94,
            "text": "TG Jesus Christ, Creator; Man, Physical Creation of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 27
          },
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 28
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Where there is neither Greek nor Jew, circumcision nor uncircumcision, Barbarian, Scythian, bond nor free: but Christ is all, and in all.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "1 Cor. 12:13."
          },
          {
            "start": 38,
            "end": 50,
            "text": "TG Circumcision."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 97,
            "end": 100
          },
          {
            "start": 118,
            "end": 120
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Put on therefore, as the elect of God, holy and beloved, bowels of mercies, kindness, humbleness of mind, meekness, longsuffering;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 30,
            "text": "TG Election."
          },
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "Gal. 5:22."
          },
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 74,
            "text": "TG Mercy."
          },
          {
            "start": 76,
            "end": 84,
            "text": "TG Benevolence."
          },
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 96,
            "text": "TG Humility."
          },
          {
            "start": 106,
            "end": 114,
            "text": "TG Meek."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Forbearing one another, and forgiving one another, if any man have a quarrel against any: even as Christ forgave you, so also do ye.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "TG Forbear."
          },
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "Mosiah 26:31 (30–31)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 126,
            "end": 128
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And above all these things put on charity, which is the bond of perfectness.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 41,
            "text": "TG Charity."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 33
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And let the peace of God rule in your hearts, to the which also ye are called in one body; and be ye thankful.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 17,
            "text": "TG Peace of God."
          },
          {
            "start": 101,
            "end": 109,
            "text": "TG Thanksgiving."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Let the word of Christ dwell in you richly in all wisdom; teaching and admonishing one another in psalms and hymns and spiritual songs, singing with grace in your hearts to the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 12,
            "text": "2 Ne. 32:3."
          },
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 56,
            "text": "TG God, Intelligence of."
          },
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 66,
            "text": "TG Teaching."
          },
          {
            "start": 109,
            "end": 114,
            "text": "TG Singing."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And whatsoever ye do in word or deed, do all in the name of the Lord Jesus, giving thanks to God and the Father by him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 38,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "1 Cor. 10:31."
          },
          {
            "start": 83,
            "end": 89,
            "text": "Col. 1:12. TG Prayer."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 38,
            "end": 40
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Wives, submit yourselves unto your own husbands, as it is fit in the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5,
            "text": "TG Marriage, Wives."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Husbands, love your wives, and be not bitter against them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "TG Marriage, Husbands."
          },
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "TG Marriage, Continuing Courtship in."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 19
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Children, obey your parents in all things: for this is well pleasing unto the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "TG Children; Family, Love within."
          },
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "TG Family, Children, Duties of; Honoring Father and Mother."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 19
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Fathers, provoke not your children to anger, lest they be discouraged.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 7,
            "text": "TG Family, Children, Responsibilities toward."
          },
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "TG Provoking."
          },
          {
            "start": 38,
            "end": 43,
            "text": "TG Anger."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 38
          },
          {
            "start": 38,
            "end": 43
          },
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 44
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Servants, obey in all things your masters according to the flesh; not with eyeservice, as menpleasers; but in singleness of heart, fearing God:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "1 Tim. 6:1 (1–2); Titus 2:9 (9–10); 1 Pet. 2:18."
          },
          {
            "start": 110,
            "end": 120,
            "text": "TG Sincere."
          },
          {
            "start": 131,
            "end": 138,
            "text": "TG Reverence."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 33
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And whatsoever ye do, do it heartily, as to the Lord, and not unto men;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "TG Commitment; Industry; Laziness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 27
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Knowing that of the Lord ye shall receive the reward of the inheritance: for ye serve the Lord Christ.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 41,
            "text": "Eph. 6:8."
          },
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 52,
            "text": "TG Reward."
          },
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 71,
            "text": "TG Inheritance."
          },
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 85,
            "text": "1 Cor. 7:22."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But he that doeth wrong shall receive for the wrong which he hath done: and there is no respect of persons.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 23,
            "text": "TG Injustice."
          },
          {
            "start": 88,
            "end": 95,
            "text": "D&C 1:35; 38:16."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
